    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/executive-assistant-to-the-office-of-the-president/1209/100174006016": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant to the Office of the President",
      "description": "Executive Assistant to the Office of the President at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Executive Assistant to the Office of the President Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20180367 Category Administrative Support Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The USC Office of the President supports the university president in leading the university and its health system, and helps advance the president’s strategic priorities in education, research, engagement, and innovation. The Office of the President plays a critically important role in welcoming and aligning stakeholders across the university and the broader community to advance USC's mission. The Executive Assistant to the Office of the President provides high-level executive support to the President, enabling effective leadership, decision-making and execution of institutional priorities. The Executive Assistant  directs complex administrative functions ensuring alignment of activities, information and resources across internal and external stakeholders and leads coordination of executive workflows and communications to optimize use of the President’s time and advance organizational objectives. While Reporting to the Chief of Staff with functional direct reporting to the President, the Executive Assistant collaborates closely with the Chief of Staff and senior leadership to manage priorities, resolve issues and support enterprise-wide planning and governance activities. closely with the Chief of Staff to manage priorities and resolve issues and support enterprise-wide planning and governance activities. Job Responsibilities: Directs strategic calendar planning and scheduling logistics for the President’s engagements. Evaluates requests and opportunities against institutional priorities to optimize allocation of the President’s time and attention. Coordinates with the chief of staff to resolve calendar conflicts, sequence engagements and anticipate future commitments. Ensures scheduling decisions support strategic objectives and enable effective participation in key events and initiatives. Designs and delivers comprehensive executive briefings, supports informed engagement and decision-making. Compiles relevant materials, background information and contextual insights for meetings, events and public appearances. Monitors quality and completeness of briefing materials and provides guidance to contributing offices as needed. Coordinates travel logistics, itineraries and on-site arrangements to ensure seamless execution of engagements and any related issues. Manages correspondence and communications workflows to support accuracy, confidentiality and responsiveness. Reviews, prioritizes and routes incoming communications to the presidential email account, determining appropriate actions and identifying stakeholders for follow-up. Oversees follow-up and responses through the Action Request System. Drafts and edits correspondence, briefing materials and responses on behalf of executive leadership. Maintains consistent standards for tone, format and documentation of sensitive and high-visibility communications. Manages all expense reimbursements on behalf of the President. Coordinates the President’s Special Advisor’s availability and travel for participation in events. Manages the Special Advisor’s travel calendar, prepares travel itineraries and briefings. Demonstrates fluency in artificial intelligence (AI) technologies and applications, with the ability to leverage AI tools to improve productivity, streamline workflows, enhance decision-making, and identify innovative solutions while exercising sound judgment, maintaining data privacy, and adhering to organizational policies. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree; Combined experience/education as substitute for minimum education 10 years of related work experience Demonstrated ability to exercise sound judgment and independent decision-making in high-pressure, high-visibility environments. Proven ability to interpret executive priorities and translate them into actionable direction. Capability to influence outcomes across diverse stakeholders. Ability to support strategic planning and execute long-term initiatives. Advanced skill in synthesizing complex information into clear, actionable insights. Proven ability to lead complex, cross-functional projects from planning through execution. Strong prioritization and organizational skills to manage multiple competing demands. Exceptional written and oral communication skills, with experience with executive correspondence and briefings. Expertise in managing complex executive operations, including calendars, workflows and information flow. Ability to navigate complex organizational dynamics and maintain effective relationships at all levels. Preferred Qualifications: 15 years of related work experience Knowledge of board governance practices and executive office protocols. Experience operating within large, complex organizations (e.g., higher education, government). Demonstrated analytical capability to inform executive-level recommendations. Strong executive presence and professional credibility in high-level interactions. Ability to adapt quickly to ambiguity and shifting priorities with resilience and composure. This position's annual base salary range is $144,730 - $160,000. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, essential skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Addtional Education Requirements Combined experience/education as substitute for minimum education Job ID REQ20180367 Posted Date 09/04/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC News Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC and SoCal Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Mission USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Artic