    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/associate-director-international-recruitment/1209/100127669856": {
      "title": "Associate Director International Recruitment",
      "description": "Associate Director International Recruitment at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Associate Director International Recruitment Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20180184 Category Nursing Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) Associate Director of International Admission The USC Office of Undergraduate Admission is seeking an Associate Director, International Admission to provide strategic and operational leadership for USC’s international undergraduate recruitment and admission efforts. The Associate Director of International Admission provides strategic and operational leadership for USC's international undergraduate recruitment and admission efforts. The position develops and implements international recruitment strategies; oversees recruitment activities and partnerships across key global markets; provides expertise in international credential evaluation and educational systems; and supports the development, implementation, and consistent application of admission policies and procedures for international applicants. The Associate Director serves as a senior resource for complex international admission cases and leads training and professional development related to international application review. The position uses enrollment data and market intelligence to evaluate recruitment effectiveness, identify opportunities for enrollment growth, and inform the allocation of recruitment resources. The Associate Director also manages assigned staff, programs, budgets, and operational processes and represents USC with schools, counselors, professional organizations, and university partners in the United States and abroad. Key Responsibilities Develop and execute international undergraduate recruitment strategies in partnership with admission leadership. Set goals for assigned international territories and evaluate recruitment, admission, yield, and enrollment outcomes. Build and maintain relationships with schools, counselors, educational organizations, alumni, and other international partners. Serve as a resource on international educational systems, credentials, grading practices, accreditation, English-language proficiency, and document authenticity. Research emerging educational systems and develop training and resources to support consistent and equitable application review. Review complex international applications, make admission decisions, and provide guidance on borderline or exception cases. Interpret admission policies and counsel prospective students and families on admission requirements and processes. Analyze enrollment data and market trends to identify opportunities and improve international recruitment and conversion strategies. Support development of recruitment communications, presentations, marketing materials, and outreach initiatives. Represent USC through presentations, recruitment events, and engagement with students, families, counselors, and university partners. Recruit, train, supervise, and develop staff, including providing performance feedback and professional development opportunities. Manage assigned programs, operational processes, resources, and budgets. Maintain knowledge of international admission trends and best practices through professional associations and industry engagement. Application Requirements Please submit cover letter and resume as part of your application. Preferred Education: Master's degree In addition, the successful candidate must also demonstrate, through ideas, words and actions, a strong commitment to USC’s Unifying Values . The salary range for this position is $85,000 - $98,000. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. #LI-AW1 Minimum Education: Bachelor's degree \nAdditional Education Requirements Combined experience/education as substitute for minimum education \nMinimum Experience: 3 years \nMinimum Skills: Lead or supervisory recruitment and admissions experience with knowledge of financial aid policies. Job ID REQ20180184 Posted Date 09/03/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC News Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC and SoCal Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Mission USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Conte